---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { contactEmail, legal } from "../config";
import "../styles/legal.css";

const toc = [["The short version", "the-short-version"], ["What I collect and why", "what-i-collect-and-why"], ["Services that handle data for me", "services-that-handle-data-for-me"], ["Cookies", "cookies"], ["How long I keep it", "how-long-i-keep-it"], ["Your rights", "your-rights"], ["Changes", "changes"]];
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data graholskis.com collects, why, and what rights you have." kit>
  <section class="pg-section pg-dark glow lg-hero">
    <div class="pg-container">
      <span class="pg-pill pg-pill-soft">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="pg-h1">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="pg-small lg-updated">Last updated {legal.updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pg-section">
    <div class="pg-container lg-layout">
      <nav class="lg-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <p class="pg-label">On this page</p>
        <ul>{toc.map(([t, id]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{t}</a></li>)}</ul>
      </nav>
      <article class="lg-prose">
    <p>
      This policy explains what personal data graholskis.com collects, why, and what you can ask me to do with it.
      The site is run by {legal.owner}, based in {legal.country}, who is responsible for your data as the data controller.
      For any question about your data, email <a class="pg-link" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="the-short-version">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The site has no analytics, no advertising and no tracking cookies.</li>
      <li>I only receive personal data when you send it to me: through the contact form, a self-check request, a booked call or a purchase.</li>
      <li>I use it to reply to you and to deliver what you asked for. I do not sell it or share it for marketing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what-i-collect-and-why">What I collect and why</h2>
    <h3>Contact form</h3>
    <p>
      Your name, company, email address and, if you add one, your message. I use them to reply. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in answering
      your enquiry, or the steps you ask for before we agree on any work (GDPR Article 6(1)(f) and 6(1)(b)).
    </p>
    <h3>Self-check request</h3>
    <p>
      Your email address, so I can send you the AI maturity self-check. The legal basis is delivering what you requested
      (Article 6(1)(b)). Requesting the self-check does not subscribe you to a newsletter.
    </p>
    <h3>Booking a call</h3>
    <p>
      Calls are booked through Calendly. You enter your details on Calendly's page, and I receive your name, email address,
      the time you chose and any answers you give. I use them to prepare for and hold the call (Article 6(1)(b)).
    </p>
    <h3>Buying a resource</h3>
    <p>
      Paid resources are sold through Lemon Squeezy, which acts as the merchant of record and handles payment, tax and invoices.
      I receive your name, email address and order details, and never see your card details. I use them to deliver the product
      and support you (Article 6(1)(b)), and keep order records as accounting law requires (Article 6(1)(c)).
    </p>
    <h3>Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Like any website, the hosting provider records technical data when a page is requested: IP address, browser type, the page
      and the time. This is used to run and secure the site (Article 6(1)(f)) and is kept for a short period by the host.
    </p>

    <h2 id="services-that-handle-data-for-me">Services that handle data for me</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Railway</strong> hosts the site and its server logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> delivers contact form and self-check requests to my email inbox.</li>
      <li><strong>Calendly</strong> handles call bookings.</li>
      <li><strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong> handles payments for paid resources.</li>
      <li><strong>YouTube</strong> (Google) plays the embedded videos.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these providers are based in the United States. Where data leaves the EU, the transfer relies on safeguards such as
      the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The site itself sets no cookies. Videos are embedded in YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com), so YouTube does
      not set cookies until you press play. Once you play a video, Google may set cookies and collect data under its own privacy policy.
      Calendly and Lemon Squeezy set their own cookies when you use their pages.
    </p>

    <h2 id="how-long-i-keep-it">How long I keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Messages and booking details are kept for as long as needed to handle your request and any follow-up, and deleted at the latest
      24 months after our last contact. Purchase records are kept for as long as accounting law requires.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask me to show you the data I hold about you, correct it, delete it, limit how I use it, or send it to you in a portable
      format. You can also object to processing based on legitimate interest. Email <a class="pg-link" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
      and I will reply within one month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you think your data has been handled wrongly, you can complain to the data protection authority in your country{
        legal.country === "Latvia" && (
          <>, or in Latvia to the Data State Inspectorate (<a class="pg-link" href="https://www.dvi.gov.lv" rel="noopener" target="_blank">dvi.gov.lv</a>)</>
        )
      }.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new date at the top.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
